Lee Gillie wrote:
> 
> I've developed some software using VMS/UCX with the asynchronous
> QIO interface.  A client would like to use the same on their system
> running VMS/TCPWARE, which I've never worked with.  They say from
> their documentation that a QIO interface is provided.  I haven't
> seen this first hand yet.
> 
> I'm wondering how similar these two are.  Should I expect source-code
> level compatibility?  Has anyone had experience doing this type of
> port that can offer insights, suggestions, tips, problems to
> anticipate?
> 
Yes, TCPware's (and MultiNet's) UCX emulation should be virtually
identical to the UCX BG $QIO interface.  We do our best to ensure
100% compatibility.  The images produced under UCX should run
without change under both TCPware and Multinet.
