I don't know if there were hardware handbooks or not.  When I worked at DEC
in the summer of 1991, one of the nice benefits was access to free printed
documentation.  It was a district sales office, so we kept several copies
of everything "usual" around in case a customer wanted one in a hurry.  I
managed to get one of everything we had; I've got most of the books in
my parents' basement with my 11/750.

I'm pretty sure that I did *not* get hardware handbooks covering the 4000,
6000, or the newer 3100 models.  Actually, I'm sure enough that I didn't
look last time the subject came up; perhaps I ought to.  I do have hardware
handbooks for... well, unfortunately, for most of what NetBSD already
runs on. :-)

Also, later hardware handbooks seem a lot less useful than the original
1/7XX and 8[68]X0 ones.  I have what appears to be the "hardware handbook"
equivalent for the 9000 series, and it pretty much only discusses possible
configurations; no detailed processor info.

I don't have a particularly new VMS fiche set, and I have no idea what the
restrictions on using that information are.  Perhaps someone from DEC can
tell us, or perhaps even help get the right documentation?

