If you've developed your program to use the TCP/IP Services for OpenVMS
(UCX) interface (either QIOs directly or by using the C Socket routines),
this program should run unchanged (same .EXE) on TCPware (and MultiNet).

Now, that said, it is worth testing to make sure that all is well.

All of the TCP/IP for OpenVMS stacks support "UCX Emulation" which allows
you to run most anything developed for UCX on other stacks. (There are
sometimes issues with installation procedures and the such that might
assume a particular stack.)

- Bernie Volz
