Hans,

> Can I download the SoftFont, save it in the LN17ps and avoid
> downloading the SoftFont for each job?

Unfortunately, no.  The SoftFont fonts are not PostScript fonts and
can't be stored in a PostScript printer.  Even if they were, the DCPS
ANSI translator does not look for PostScript fonts when using SoftFont
fonts.  You can buy a hard disk for the LN17ps but it will not be
helpful in your situation.

Do you know for sure that your performance problem is due to the
downloading of these fonts?  It is possible that a slower OpenVMS system
could take a while processing SoftFont fonts.

> Also, are the DCPS-OPEN and DCPS-PLUS 1.4 and 1.5 licenses still in
> the DEC Campus program?

I believe they are.  When DIGITAL sold the printer business to GENICOM,
it was stated that there would be no change in packaging or licensing
for DCPS software or licenses.

