In article <aus-1604981414220001@wvia41.virologie.uni-wuerzburg.de>,
  aus@vim.uni-wuerzburg.de (Hans M. Aus) wrote:

> Does anyone know if printing several files which use SoftFonts is faster
> with DCPS 1.4 than it is with DCPS 1.3?
> The problem in DCPS 1.3 seems to be that DCPS loads the SoftFont library
> everytime a print job starts on the LN17ps. This makes printing much
> slower on the LN17ps then it is on the LN08 with the font cartridge.

SoftFont behavior has not changed in DCPS V1.4, nor in V1.5.  There are
no plans to change the behavior in any future version of DCPS.

DCPS sends every font requested by the user via /PARAMETERS=FONTS_USED
to the printer once per ANSI file in a print job, regardless of whether
the font is referenced in the file.

So, fonts that are resident in the printer on the LN08 are being sent
from the host when using SoftFonts, and performance is affected.  The
faster LN17ps may in fact print these jobs more slowly than the LN08.

I'd suggest not specifying fonts not actually used in a job, so fonts
are not needlessly sent to the printer.

